# Copy to .dev.vars for local development. Everything here is optional.
#
# Domain inboxes receive mail at. Defaults to the host of SITE_URL, then the host the UI is
# opened on (localhost in `npm run dev`).
# MAIL_DOMAIN=mail.example.com
# Public origin for canonical/Open Graph URLs. Defaults to the request origin.
# SITE_URL=https://mail.example.com
#
# Optional: create a per-address Email Routing rule whenever an inbox is opened.
# Both must be set, otherwise inboxes are just opened (rely on a catch-all rule instead).
# CF_TOKEN needs "Zone > Email Routing Rules > Edit" on ZONE_ID.
# In production: npx wrangler secret put ZONE_ID && npx wrangler secret put CF_TOKEN
# ZONE_ID=<your-zone-id>
# CF_TOKEN=<your-api-token>
# Worker that the rules send mail to (defaults to "maildrop").
# EMAIL_WORKER_NAME=maildrop
# Enables POST /api/admin/cleanup (deletes all inboxes and their routing rules).
# Use a long random value, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`. The route returns 404 when unset.
# ADMIN_TOKEN=
